    "result_text": "All 269 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created (or otherwise mapped to a response), the response now includes an `initials` field with the first letters of the first and last name, upper-cased and dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `G.T.`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto`, mirroring the existing `displayName` pattern, with an `initials(owner)` helper that combines the upper-cased first character of the first and last names, each followed by a dot. Null/empty names contribute nothing (no dot), keeping it robust.\n\n3. **`src/test/java/.../OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 Extended `createOwnerSuccess` to assert `$.initials` equals `G.T.` for owner George Testowner.\n\nThe `initials` field flows through automatically to the create-owner (`addOwner`) response as well as get/list, since they all use `toOwnerDto`.",
